# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901>)

ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1868919/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A number of large studies and consortia have been established that aim to identify genetic modifiers of cancer risk in BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation carriers, including Modifiers and Genetics in Cancer (MAGIC), Epidemiological study of BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation carriers (EMBRACE), Genetic Modifiers of cancer risk in BRCA1/2 mutation carriers (GEMO), the Kathleen Cuningham Consortium for Research into Familial Breast Cancer (kConFab), the German Consortium for Hereditary Breast and Ovarian Cancer (GCHBOC) and the Breast Cooperative Family Registry (Breast-CFR). However, with current sample sizes of less than 1,500 carriers, none of these groups have adequate power to identify genetic modifiers with confidence. To address this problem, a 'consortium of consortia', the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 (CIMBA), was established in 2005 (see Additional file 1 for a list of current contributors).") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001094>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8755508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Male BRCA1 and BRCA2 pathogenic variant carriers were recruited through 40 studies from 19 countries participating in the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 (CIMBA) (24).") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001526>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9537519/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CIMBA phenotype data used in this study from BCFR-AU, BCFR-NC, BCFR-NY, BCFR-PA, BCFR-UT, BFBOCC, BIDMC, BMBSA, CBCS, CNIO, COH, DEMOKRITOS, DFCI, FCCC, GEORGETOWN, HCSC, HRBCP, HUNBOCS, HVH, ICO, KCONFAB, KUMC, MAYO, MSKCC, MUV, NCI, NNPIO, NORTHSHORE, OSUCCG, PBCS, SMC, SWE-BRCA, UCHICAGO, UCSF, UPENN, UPITT, UTMDACC, VFCTG, and WCP studies are available in the dbGaP database under accession code phs001321.v1.p1.") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001539>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7890067/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CIMBA DACC approval is required to access data from studies BCFR-ON, BRICOH, CONSIT TEAM, DKFZ, EMBRACE, FPGMX, G-FAST, GC-HBOC, GEMO, HEBCS, HEBON, IHCC, INHERIT, IOVHBOCS, MCGILL, NRG_ONCOLOGY, OUH and UKGRFOCR (see Supplementary Table 1—for a list of all CIMBA studies).") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001621>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9537519/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CIMBA phenotype data used in this study from BCFR-AU, BCFR-NC, BCFR-NY, BCFR-PA, BCFR-UT, BFBOCC, BIDMC, BMBSA, CBCS, CNIO, COH, DEMOKRITOS, DFCI, FCCC, GEORGETOWN, HCSC, HRBCP, HUNBOCS, HVH, ICO, KCONFAB, KUMC, MAYO, MSKCC, MUV, NCI, NNPIO, NORTHSHORE, OSUCCG, PBCS, SMC, SWE-BRCA, UCHICAGO, UCSF, UPENN, UPITT, UTMDACC, VFCTG, and WCP studies are available in the dbGaP database under accession code phs001321.v1.p1.") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001623>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7890067/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CIMBA DACC approval is required to access data from studies BCFR-ON, BRICOH, CONSIT TEAM, DKFZ, EMBRACE, FPGMX, G-FAST, GC-HBOC, GEMO, HEBCS, HEBON, IHCC, INHERIT, IOVHBOCS, MCGILL, NRG_ONCOLOGY, OUH and UKGRFOCR (see Supplementary Table 1—for a list of all CIMBA studies).") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001928>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7808397/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CIMBA DACC approval is required to access data from the BCFR-ON, CONSIT TEAM, DKFZ, EMBRACE, FPGMX, GC-HBOC, GEMO, G-FAST, HEBCS, HEBON, IHCC, INHERIT, IOVHBOCS, IPOBCS, MCGILL, MODSQUAD, NAROD, OCGN, OUH and UKGRFOCR studies (Supplementary Table 3).") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000901> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001932>)

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000905> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000905>)

ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9810640/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Fourteen population-based CREAM cohorts that had exome chip genotypes on individuals with refractive error measurements were used in this study. These 14 cohorts were: Singapore Chinese Eye Study (SCES), Singapore Malay Eye Study (SiMES), Singapore Indian Eye Study (SINDI), Age Related Eye Study (AREDS)") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000905> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9810640/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Fourteen population-based CREAM cohorts that had exome chip genotypes on individuals with refractive error measurements were used in this study. These 14 cohorts were: Singapore Chinese Eye Study (SCES), Singapore Malay Eye Study (SiMES), Singapore Indian Eye Study (SINDI), Age Related Eye Study (AREDS), Rotterdam Study I (RSI), Erasmus Rucphen Family (ERF), Raine Eye Health Study (REHS) of the Raine Study, Beaver Dam Eye Study (BDES), Estonian Genome Center for the University of Tartu (EGCUT), Finnish Twin Study on Aging (FITSA), Ogliastra, Croatia-Korcula, TwinsUK, and EPIC-Norfolk.") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000905> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001289>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4551475/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CREAM meta-analysis included data from 32 studies: 1958 British Birth Cohort, ALSPAC (mothers), ANZRAG, AREDS1a1b, AREDS1c, Beijing Eye Study, BMES, CROATIA-Korcula, CROATIA-Split, CROATIA-Vis, DCCT, EGCUT, ERF, FECD, FITSA, Framingham, GHS 1, GHS 2, KORA, OGP Talana, ORCADES, RS1, RS2, RS3, SCES, SIMES, SINDI, SP2, TEST/BATS, TwinsUK, WESDR, and YFS.") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000905> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489>)

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915>)

ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985341/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cardiovascular Health Study (CHS) is a population-based cohort study of risk factors for heart disease and stroke in adults ≥65 years conducted across four field centers.") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000384>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985341/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Framingham Heart Study (FHS) is a community-based cohort that enrolled three generations of participants.") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000385>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985341/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BioVU cohort consisted of patients at Vanderbilt University Medical Center who have consented to be a part of the program.") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985341/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The deCODE Icelandic heart failure (HF) sample set included patients diagnosed with HF at Landspitali – The National University Hospital (LUH) in Reykjavik and the Primary Health Care Clinics of the Reykjavik capital region, following ICD-9 and ICD-10 codes for heart failure, as described in this manuscript.") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985341/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Henry Ford Heart Failure Pharmacogenomic Registry (HFPGR) was approved by the Institutional Review Board at the Henry Ford Health System, and all patients gave written informed consent prior to participation.") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000868>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985341/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TRIUMPH (TRanslational Initiative on Unique and novel strategies for Management of Patients with Heart failure, NTR1893), is an observational prospective study of patients admitted with acute HF in 14 hospitals in the Netherlands between September 2009 and December 2013.") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000952>)
ObjectPropertyAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8712846/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of the nine case collections, seven were primarily focused on HF while two identified HF cases from an at‐risk population (COGEN and LURIC).") <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/hasCohort> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000915> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001602>)

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000926> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000926>)

